<div class="hero">
  <div class="hero-inner">
    <div class="kicker">Case No. MLH&#8209;001 &middot; The Human Law Project</div>
    <h1>Nobody reads<br>the <span class="strike">terms and conditions</span>.<br>They read what's <mark style="background:var(--yellow);padding:2px 10px;">left of them.</mark></h1>
    <p class="sub">A research project on why law is unreadable by design, and what happens when someone actually sits down and redesigns it. Built from a year of field notes, one clause at a time, by someone who has been angry about a contract more than once.</p>
    <div class="hero-cta"><span class="stamp">Exhibit Open Below</span><span class="arrow">&darr; scroll to read the file</span></div>

    <div class="redesign-block reveal">
      <div class="redesign-bar">
        <span class="filetitle">Live Exhibit &middot; Same clause, two documents</span>
        <div class="toggle">
          <button id="btnLegal" class="active">As Written</button>
          <button id="btnHuman">Redesigned</button>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="redesign-content">
        <div class="doc legal" id="docBlock">
